            <ArticleTitle>Emergence of low-molecular-weight heparins in cardiology.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>141S-146S</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Drug therapy for the management of acute coronary syndromes is rapidly expanding. Over the past few years, a number of new antithrombotic agents have been introduced, including low-molecular-weight heparins. The epidemiology and pathophysiology of acute coronary syndromes are discussed, with a historical perspective on the use of antithrombotic therapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
